# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Neura — environment template
#
#  Copy to `.env.local` and fill in your own keys:
#      cp .env.example .env.local      (macOS / Linux / Git Bash)
#      Copy-Item .env.example .env.local   (PowerShell)
#
#  `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
#
#  Every variable here is read on the SERVER only. Never prefix one
#  with NEXT_PUBLIC_: that inlines the value into the browser bundle
#  and publishes the key to every visitor.
#
#  Leave a placeholder as-is if you have no key yet. The app rejects
#  any value containing "PASTE_", so an untouched template is treated
#  as "not configured" and the request falls through to the next
#  provider rather than failing on a fake key.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Lesson generation ─────────────────────────────────────────
#  Read in: src/lib/lesson-json.ts, src/lib/lesson-generator.ts
#
#  Targets are tried in order and the first that returns a usable
#  lesson wins. Setting only OPENROUTER_API_KEY is enough: the model
#  chain below rotates through several models on that one key.


# 1) PRIMARY — OpenRouter. One key covers generation and voice.
#    Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=PASTE_your_openrouter_key_here


# 2) MODEL CHAIN
#    Tried in order on the OpenRouter key above; first usable
#    lesson wins. All are available on one key:
#      gemma-4-31b-it -> gemma-4-26b-a4b-it
#      -> nemotron-3.5-lightning -> qwen3.8-27b
#    Add one model to the FRONT of the chain without losing the
#    built-in fallbacks:
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it

#    Off by default: free-tier models are rate-limited to about 50
#    requests a day and their structured-JSON output is weaker.
# NEURA_ALLOW_FREE_MODELS=false


# 3) SELF-HOSTED — put ahead of every hosted provider.
#    Any OpenAI-compatible server works (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama,
#    LM Studio, TGI). This is what makes data residency a config
#    change rather than a code change.
#    Falls back to OPENROUTER_API_KEY if its own key is unset.
# NEURA_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# NEURA_LLM_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-8b
# NEURA_LLM_API_KEY=PASTE_your_self_host_key_here

#    Set to false for servers that reject the json_object hint.
# NEURA_LLM_JSON_HINT=true


# 4) PROVIDER TIMEOUT
#    Raise for large self-hosted models running on CPU.
#    Default 45000.
# NEURA_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=45000


# ── Narration voice ───────────────────────────────────────────
#  Read in: src/lib/openrouter-tts.ts, src/lib/tts-voice.ts
#
#  Narration runs through the OpenRouter key above. Without it,
#  narration still works using the browser's built-in speech
#  synthesis, which sounds noticeably flatter.
#
#  Accepted values (VoiceMode in src/lib/tts-voice.ts):
#    "auto"       - expressive, degrading to standard then budget as
#                   models become unavailable. Default.
#    "expressive" - Gemini TTS for story narration, Voxtral for the
#                   emotional beats (praise, hints, questions). Most
#                   natural, and what the app uses by default.
#    "standard"   - Voxtral for everything. Fewer round trips, no
#                   Gemini request.
#    "budget"     - hosted Kokoro for everything. Cheapest, flattest.
# NEURA_TTS_MODE=auto

#    Local Kokoro is NOT a server mode: it runs in the browser and is
#    feature-detected at runtime (see src/lib/say.ts), so there is no
#    environment variable for it.

#    Per-request speech timeout. Default 25000.
# NEURA_TTS_TIMEOUT_MS=25000


# ── Legacy providers ──────────────────────────────────────────
#  Optional extra failovers for lesson generation. The model chain
#  above already rotates within OpenRouter, so these only help if
#  OpenRouter itself is unreachable.

#    Key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=PASTE_your_groq_key_here

#    Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=PASTE_your_gemini_key_here


# ── Attribution ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Sent as the OpenRouter HTTP-Referer header on server calls.
# NEURA_SITE_URL=https://neuraai-liard.vercel.app